WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.340
We could say many bad things about Russia,&nbsp;
but they have one very good thing that must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.240
be recognized. If the golden rule of&nbsp;
any casino is "the dealer always wins",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.060
in the energy game it is Russia that always wins.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.360
It is by far the largest country&nbsp;
in the world and, what’s more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.920
its territory is full of natural resources,&nbsp;
which gives it a huge competitive advantage.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.200
Just think of the world's fourth largest economy,&nbsp;
Germany. A lot of Volkswagens and a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.300
Siemens, but for decades Germany has depended&nbsp;
on Russian gas for abundant and cheap energy.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.320
As you know, all this blew up with the Russian&nbsp;
invasion of Ukraine. And not surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.900
it has been very difficult&nbsp;
to find alternatives. One of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.080
the biggest problems is Germany's&nbsp;
reluctance to use nuclear power.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.280
Last April they shut down their last&nbsp;
three nuclear power plants. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.080
there are many experts who stress that this&nbsp;
was a mistake, that nuclear energy could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.980
an alternative to natural gas and a way&nbsp;
to completely avoid dependence on Russia.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.040
But wait a minute because we are&nbsp;
talking about energy. And in this game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.920
you know what we said, Russia always wins.
 &nbsp;

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:10.380
With 37 reactors, Russia is not only&nbsp;
the country in the world fourth on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.520
list for the most nuclear reactors. It&nbsp;
also dominates the nuclear fuel market.
 &nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.600
You see, although its uranium mines account&nbsp;
for barely 5% of the planet's production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:26.040
Rosatom's global share in the uranium conversion&nbsp;
process rises to 27% and soars to 46% in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.520
of uranium enrichment capacity.
 
This explains, as we told you here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.720
on VisualPolitik last February, why&nbsp;
the West does not impose sanctions on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:39.180
Russia's state-owned atomic energy corporation.
 
Now, just as LNG has offered the major alternative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.940
to Russian gas, with nuclear fuel there is another&nbsp;
alternative, which is France: a country that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:49.020
a long nuclear tradition and could be an&nbsp;
important option for the West to consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.640
if it seeks to reduce dependence on Russia.
 
In Paris, they are clear about their strategy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.260
They want to proceed. But they have some stumbling&nbsp;
blocks to get past. The main one is that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.480
French nuclear sector has been in a permanent&nbsp;
crisis for 15 years. When it puts out one fire, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:08.640
immediately starts another. And the latest one has&nbsp;
been in a place as far away as it was unexpected.
 &nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.920
